BEGIN_PGML A definite integral is given below. As demonstrated in Examples[$NBSP]*1.3.18 and 1.3.19, do the following: a. Find a formula to approximate the definite integral using [`n`] subintervals and the provided rule.
a. Evaluate the formula using [`n=10\text{,}`] [`100\text{,}`] and [`1000\text{.}`]
a. Find the limit of the formula, as [`n\to \infty\text{,}`] to find the exact value of the definite integral.
[`\ds \int_{0}^{1} \left([$f]\right)\, dx\text{,}`] using the [$rule].
[@KeyboardInstructions('Enter the formula in terms of [`n`] here.')@]**
